The seeding (DEBUG AppModel.enterMultiHostDemo, synthetic only) wipes the
simulator's profile store and creates three profiles: Host A (live active
store; rows = demo-orbit blocked + demo-atlas working + demo-ledger idle),
Host B (pinned; coordinator session store holds RETAINED rows with ts ~6m
old, store connection error "host unreachable"), Host C (pinned, then
connection state set to key mismatch — no session, fails closed). Host A and
Host B share raw agent id herdr:demo-orbit-blocked and the demo-orbit /
demo-atlas repos. Fingerprint fixture keys: Data(repeating: n, count: 32)
base64 for n in 9..12 (host A/B/C + add-host) — synthetic, never a real key.

